# Rule hardening: every code example (v0.6.0-alpha.3 and alpha.4)

Two kinds of examples per rule: adversarial cases that now live as permanent tests in `tests/*.test.js`, and real Youmotion code the redesigned rules were validated against (branch state on 2026-09-04).

## 1. `no-implicit-external-dependencies` (alpha.3)

Adversarial tests, all groups detected:

```ts
const a = () => new Date();                 // TimeDep
const b = () => performance.now();          // TimeDep
const c = () => Math.random();              // RandomDep
const d = () => crypto.randomUUID();        // RandomDep
const e = () => process.env.API_URL;        // ConfigDep
const f = () => fetch("/api");              // FetchDep
const g = () => new WebSocket("wss://x");   // FetchDep
const h = () => localStorage.getItem("k");  // StorageDep
const i = () => document.cookie;            // StorageDep
const j = () => new Intl.DateTimeFormat();  // LocaleDep
const k = () => navigator.language;         // LocaleDep
```

Pure or type-only forms are ignored:

```ts
const parse = (value: string) => new Date(value);
type Clock = { readonly now: typeof Date.now };
const typed = (client: WebSocket, formatter: Intl.DateTimeFormat) => [client, formatter];
const fetch = (url: string) => url;      // local shadow
const call = () => fetch("/local");
```

Factories are derived from the dependency name, so no `factories` list is needed:

```ts
const createRandom = (): Random => ({ next: () => Math.random() });
const createTestFetch = () => ({ fetch: (url: string) => fetch(url) });
class Config { static createConfig() { return process.env; } }
```

Custom capabilities extend the built-ins instead of replacing them. Before alpha.3 the Youmotion config below silently dropped the logger check:

```js
capabilities: [{ selector: "Platform.now", dependency: "PlatformTimeDep", replacement: "deps.platformTime.now()" }]
// Date.now, console.log, Platform.now are all reported now. Use `groups: []` to opt out of built-ins.
```

Real Youmotion findings (application layer, no injected clock or random source):

```ts
// src/features/reminders/application/reminder-coordinator.ts:68
id: existing?.id ?? createReminderAssignmentId({ timestamp: now.getTime(), nonce: Math.random().toString(16).slice(2) }),
// :125
const now = ReminderTimestamp.make(new Date().toISOString());
```

## 2. `no-exported-dependency-instances` (alpha.3)

Concept: a module-level instance created at import time by a constructor or factory verb, exported in any shape.

```ts
export const logger = createLogger();
export const db = createDb("url");
export const clock = new Time();
export const appSettingsStore = createAppSettingsStore();
export const client = makeClient();
export const connection = openConnection();
export let socket = new WebSocket("wss://example");
const store = xstate.createStore({ context: {} });
const frozen = Object.freeze(createRegistry());
const awaited = await createConnection();
const typed = createCache() as Cache;
export { store as appStore, frozen, awaited, typed };
export default createRouter();
const queryClient = new QueryClient();
export default queryClient;
```

Allowed: factories, lazy access, pure results, definition factories, and instances inside functions.

```ts
export const createLogger = (): Logger => ({ log: console.log });
export const parsed = parseConfig();
export const lazy = () => createDb();
export const ThemeContext = createContext(null);
export const styles = StyleSheet.create({ root: { flex: 1 } });
export const createDeps = () => { const logger = createLogger(); return { logger }; };
```

Real Youmotion findings (three application stores exported as import-time singletons):

```ts
// src/features/analytics/application/analytics.store.ts:23
export const analyticsStore = createStore({ ... });
// src/features/check-in/application/check-in-history.store.ts:45
export const checkInHistoryStore = createStore({ ... });
// src/features/check-in/application/history-timeframe.store.ts:24
export const historyTimeframeStore = createStore({ ... });
```

## 3. `no-namespace-exports` (alpha.3)

Reported only when an object bundles behavior:

```ts
export const Utils = { ok, trySync };
export const api = { load: async () => null, save() {} };
export const wrapped = Object.freeze({ run: () => 1 } as const);
export default { parse: () => 1 };
export namespace Utils { export const ok = () => true; }
```

Data objects are no longer reported. These shapes came straight from Youmotion:

```ts
export const tabScreenContentStyle = { paddingHorizontal: 16, gap: 8 };           // src/components/ui/tab-screen-layout.ts
export const ReduceMotion = { Always: "always", Never: "never" };                  // src/testing/react-native-reanimated.harness.tsx
export const occurrenceTimeDatabaseMigration = { id: "...", statements: [...] };  // src/features/check-in/infrastructure/migrations
export const onboardingExampleSelection = { emotion: EMOTIONS.calm, beliefs: [a, b] };
export const Card = { Root, Title };  // compound component API, allowed by default
```

## 4. Assertion rules: `require-assertions`, `require-contract-assertions`, `no-unasserted-return` (alpha.4)

Assertions are recognized structurally. None of these need `assertionNames`:

```ts
import { strict as invariant } from "node:assert";
import nodeAssert from "node:assert";
import * as a from "assert";
import { check } from "../shared/assert.ts";
import assert from "@/assert";                       // Youmotion's own helper module
const alias = nodeAssert;

const parse = (input: string) => {
  invariant(input.length > 0);
  nodeAssert.ok(input !== "x");
  a.strictEqual(typeof input, "string");
  alias.ok(input);
  check(input);
  assert(input);
  return input;
};

function assertPositive(value: number): asserts value is number { if (value <= 0) throw new Error(); }
const size = (value: number) => { assertPositive(value); return value * 2; };
```

Negative case kept: an unrelated module under an assert-like alias is not an assertion.

```ts
import { isEqual as assertEqual } from "lodash";   // not from an assertion module, not counted
```

Real validation: linting all of Youmotion with `assertionNames` removed from every rule produced zero new findings.

## 5. `require-interactive-component-contract` (alpha.4)

Works with `"error"` and no options. Spread forwarding satisfies the contract:

```jsx
function Button({ onPress, children, disabled, ...rest }) {
  return <Pressable accessibilityRole="button" onPress={onPress} {...rest}>{children}</Pressable>;
}
```

Prop aliasing and style-function feedback count:

```jsx
function Button({ disabled, onPress, label }) {
  const isDisabled = disabled;
  return (
    <Pressable
      accessibilityRole="button"
      aria-disabled={isDisabled}
      onPress={disabled ? undefined : onPress}
      style={({ pressed }) => [styles.base, pressed && styles.pressed]}
    >
      <Text>{label}</Text>
    </Pressable>
  );
}
```

Screens that merely contain buttons are not primitives. Only `Wrapped` is checked here:

```jsx
function CheckInScreen({ onSave, onCancel, title }) {
  return (
    <View>
      <Text>{title}</Text>
      <Pressable onPress={onSave}><Text>Save</Text></Pressable>
      <Pressable onPress={onCancel}><Text>Cancel</Text></Pressable>
    </View>
  );
}
const Wrapped = ({ children, onPress }) => (
  <View style={styles.wrapper}><Pressable onPress={onPress}>{children}</Pressable></View>
);
```

Real validation on Youmotion with the option object removed: 16 primitives detected, all buttons, chips, tabs, or rows. Example:

```tsx
// src/components/ui/settings-action-row.tsx:6
export function SettingsActionRow({ count, description, onPress, testID, title }: {...}) {
  // reported: missing accessibility state, disabled behavior
```

## 6. `no-over-depending` (alpha.4)

All of these are now correctly treated as use:

```ts
const a = (deps: TimeDep & LoggerDep) => { const { time } = deps; return time.now(); };   // logger reported, time not
const b = (deps: TimeDep) => { const d = deps; return d.time.now(); };                    // alias: all used
const c = (deps: TimeDep & LoggerDep) => { const { time, ...rest } = deps; return rest; }; // rest: all used
const d = (deps: TimeDep) => run(deps);                                                    // forwarded: all used
const e = (deps: TimeDep) => (inner: (deps: LoggerDep) => void) => deps.time.now();       // no cross-contamination
```

## 7. `prefer-arrow-functions` and `dependency-wrapper-shape` (alpha.4)

```ts
class Repo { getAll(): Item[] { return []; } get size() { return 0; } }   // never reported
const api = { load() { return 1; } };                                       // never reported
interface TimeDep { readonly time: Time<Utc>; }                             // type arguments allowed
```

## 8. `declarative-components` (alpha.4)

Inline JSX callbacks and hook arguments are fine. Only bound nested declarations are reported:

```jsx
const SplashScreen = () => {
  const actor = useActorRef(machine);
  const submit = () => true;                              // reported (bound declaration)
  return <Splash onReady={() => actor.send({ type: "ready" })} items={items.map((item) => <Row key={item.id} />)} />;
};
const createId = () => "x";                               // capitalized-name rule no longer applies: no JSX, not a component
```

## 9. Compound component rules (alpha.4)

```jsx
export const MathHelpers = { Root: computeRoot, Square: computeSquare };   // no JSX members: ignored
export const Accordion = Object.assign(AccordionRoot, { Item, Trigger });  // recognized as a compound
function AccordionRoot({ children }) {
  return <AccordionContext.Provider><AccordionShadowOverlay />{children}</AccordionContext.Provider>;
}
// AccordionShadowOverlay is not an Accordion member, so it is no longer reported as a root-owned part.
```

## 10. Module and safety rules (alpha.4)

```ts
import { x } from "./x.js"; export { x };            // no-barrel-files: reported
import feature from "./feature";                      // no-barrel-imports: reported when ./feature/index.ts exists
export const user = UserSchema.parse(JSON.parse(s));  // no-unvalidated-json-parse: valid via *.parse
const raw = JSON.parse(s);
if (!raw) throw new Error("empty");
export const cfg = Schema.decodeUnknownSync(T)(raw);  // guard reference tolerated
import { Effect } from "effect";
Effect.catchTag("NotFound", () => Effect.succeed(null)); // effect-error-handling: silent fallback reported
import { Effect as E } from "effect";
E.catchAll(() => E.void);                              // alias resolved, reported
```

## 11. Design-system rules (alpha.4)

```jsx
<View style={{ backgroundColor: "#8A3D35" }} />                 // no-raw-design-values: hex on a color property, no list needed
<View style={{ backgroundColor: isDark ? "#000" : "#fff" }} /> // no-raw-design-properties: conditional literals
import * as RN from "react-native"; <RN.TouchableOpacity />     // prefer-design-system-components: namespace resolved
const override = { backgroundColor: "red" }; <Button style={override} /> // no-design-identity-overrides: const resolved
```

Real Youmotion findings from the new default hex detection, all in test files:

```
